1
00:00:03,068 --> 00:00:06,781
Look: the stars are blinking, like little trembling lamps.

2
00:00:06,831 --> 00:00:09,960
That one, right at the horizon, dances even more!

3
00:00:10,010 --> 00:00:11,373
Why do stars twinkle?

4
00:00:12,151 --> 00:00:13,616
Mila notices a very bright

5
00:00:13,666 --> 00:00:15,480
dot that doesn't tremble at all.

6
00:00:15,530 --> 00:00:17,053
Noah checks: it's a planet!

7
00:00:17,103 --> 00:00:18,559
Why does it stay so calm?

8
00:00:19,332 --> 00:00:20,846
Discovery mission!

9
00:00:23,362 --> 00:00:23,893
Mini mode!

10
00:00:23,943 --> 00:00:26,450
Between the star and your eye, there is air.

11
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:30,576
And the air isn't calm: pockets of warm and cold air move all the time,

12
00:00:30,626 --> 00:00:32,253
like above a road in summer.

13
00:00:33,031 --> 00:00:35,358
Each pocket bends the light a little.

14
00:00:35,408 --> 00:00:38,377
The star is so far away that it's just a point:

15
00:00:38,427 --> 00:00:41,524
its tiny ray jumps right, left, brighter, dimmer.

16
00:00:41,574 --> 00:00:42,345
It twinkles!

17
00:00:43,111 --> 00:00:44,439
The planet, closer to us,

18
00:00:44,489 --> 00:00:46,037
is a small disk, not a point.

19
00:00:46,087 --> 00:00:48,682
Its rays pass through lots of different pockets:

20
00:00:48,732 --> 00:00:51,652
the jumps blend together, and its light stays steady.

21
00:00:52,421 --> 00:00:54,140
And up there, above the air?

22
00:00:54,190 --> 00:00:57,803
Nothing trembles anymore: the stars shine perfectly still.

23
00:00:57,853 --> 00:01:00,443
That's why we send telescopes into space.

24
00:01:01,232 --> 00:01:03,344
That's why stars twinkle.

25
00:01:04,748 --> 00:01:05,996
Stars shine steadily;

26
00:01:06,046 --> 00:01:09,631
it's the moving air above us that makes their light dance.

27
00:01:11,232 --> 00:01:12,822
With an adult, in the dark:

28
00:01:12,872 --> 00:01:16,041
shine a light on the ceiling through a bowl of water.

29
00:01:16,091 --> 00:01:18,532
Stir the water: the spot of light dances,

30
00:01:18,582 --> 00:01:19,310
like a star!

31
00:01:20,094 --> 00:01:22,129
And what is a shooting star?

32
00:01:22,179 --> 00:01:23,669
The answer tomorrow.
